# WIN-CHS_RT-SHIM-PLAN — Phase 0 follow-up, sub-agent P

File: openOODA/audit/win_chs_rt_shim_plan.oot line.
Date: 2026-08-19. Lane: read-only shim plan. Owner: ooda/runtime/ owner. Cross-ref: openOODA/audit/win_chs_rt_posix_audit.oot (B), openOODA/audit/win_chs_rt_audit_2nd.oot (J), openOODA/audit/win_compiler_plan.oot.
Scope: turn B+J's audit into a step-by-step shim plan for the runtime owner. No code change here; this is a build script for the runtime owner.

## 0. Method and inputs

- Read B's audit (154 lines, 95 POSIX surfaces, 86 direct Windows eq, 11 redesign rows).
- Read J's audit (137 lines, ~225 line-level call sites, 3 material misses vs B).
- Read chs_rt.c umbrella (40 #include of chs_rt_*.c, 1 straggler chs_rt_list_set.c). Umbrella at chs_rt.c:2-41.
- Read chs_rt.h (chs_rt.h:63-92 declares oo_str_lit, oo_str_concat, oo_str_eq, oo_str_release — the four symbols the orchestrator's first link missed). The umbrella provides them.
- Grep every chs_rt_*.c for `#include` lines. The full POSIX header set is at the end of this file in §A.1.
- Read oodac/oodac/main.oo:170-184 (the bash-ism is line 178).
- POSIX header grep across all 41 chs_rt_*.c files.

## 1. Shim order

Three phases, sequential. Each phase has a hard gate (compile, link, run). Do not skip a phase.

- Phase A — header stubs. Goal: every chs_rt_*.c compiles under mingw. Gate: gcc accepts the umbrella TU without a "fatal error: sys/...: No such file or directory".
- Phase B — function shims. Goal: every POSIX/Linux symbol the chs_rt umbrella calls is satisfied at link. Gate: gcc produces the .exe; no "undefined reference".
- Phase C — behavior shims. Goal: the 11 redesign surfaces return a correct Windows value, not a stub. Gate: hello.oo prints, Landlock returns ENOSYS, /proc reads via GetCommandLineA, setrlimit maps to Job Object.

Order rule: do A completely, then B completely, then C. Mixing them keeps the error chain noisy.

Blocker severity:
- Phase A errors are compile errors that block ALL of chs_rt. Top priority.
- Phase B errors are link errors that block the .exe. Second priority.
- Phase C is runtime correctness. Third. hello.oo will print with Phase C missing — but it will not sandbox.

## 2. Phase A — header stubs

New file: `ooda/runtime/chs_rt_win32.h` (or `chs_rt_posix_shim.h`). The runtime owner picks the name. The header is included by the umbrella chs_rt.c (at the top, after chs_rt.h) BEFORE any chs_rt_*.c #include. So every chs_rt_*.c sees the stubs.

Stubs to provide, in include order. LoC counts are approximate C lines of stub code.

| stub header | provides | calls covered | LoC | link flag |
|-------------|----------|---------------|-----|-----------|
| `sys/wait.h` | `WIFEXITED`, `WEXITSTATUS`, `WIFSIGNALED`, `WTERMSIG` as macros that read a Windows exit code word. No `pid_t` wait, just the macros. | chs_rt_sys.c:4, chs_rt_ffi_sec.c:12 | ~15 | none |
| `sys/prctl.h` | empty stub (no `prctl` on Win32). | chs_rt_landlock.c:3 | ~6 | none |
| `sys/syscall.h` | empty stub. | chs_rt_landlock.c:4 | ~6 | none |
| `sys/random.h` | declares `getentropy(buf, n)`, defined in Phase B shim. | chs_rt_meta.c:7, chs_rt_alloc.c:9, chs_rt_ffi_sec.c:15, chs_rt_time_rand.c:7 | ~10 | -lbcrypt |
| `dlfcn.h` | declares `dlopen`, `dlclose`, `dlsym`, `dlerror`, `RTLD_LAZY`, `RTLD_NOW`, `RTLD_GLOBAL`. Defined in Phase B. | chs_rt_ffi.c:5, chs_rt_ffi_sec.c:8 | ~25 | -lkernel32 |
| `strings.h` | mingw already has it (declares `bcmp`, `bcopy`, `bzero`). `explicit_bzero` is missing. Add macro. | chs_rt_crypto.c:4 | ~3 | none |
| `pthread.h` | mingw-w64 winpthreads provides it. Add `-lpthread` to link. | chs_rt_str_intern.c:4, chs_rt_list.c:2, chs_rt_ffi.c:7, chs_rt_channel.c:5, chs_rt_meta.c:5, chs_rt_alloc.c:6, chs_rt_actor.c:6, chs_rt_time_rand.c:5, chs_rt_ffi_sec.c:10, chs_rt_thread.c:4, chs_rt_libfloor.c:5 | 0 | -lpthread (winpthread) |
| `netdb.h`, `arpa/inet.h`, `netinet/in.h`, `sys/socket.h`, `sys/stat.h`, `sys/types.h`, `unistd.h`, `fcntl.h`, `dirent.h`, `errno.h`, `stdio.h`, `stdlib.h`, `string.h`, `time.h`, `limits.h`, `ctype.h`, `math.h`, `stdint.h` | mingw provides all of these. | many | 0 | none |

Total Phase A LoC: ~65 lines of header + 0 link flag for most, 3 link flags (-lbcrypt, -lkernel32, -lpthread). 4 inline shim functions defined elsewhere in Phase B.

